{
  "summary": "Preserves queued txid orphan resolution requests when a non-witness parent transaction is rejected as TX_RECONSIDERABLE. The download manager skips calling ForgetTxHash on the witness hash if a reconsiderable transaction lacks witness data. This ensures peers that announced an orphan child are still asked for the legacy parent by txid when that parent arrives first from a different peer.",
  "problem": "For non-witness transactions, the wtxid equals the txid. When a low-feerate legacy parent is rejected with TX_RECONSIDERABLE, forgetting its wtxid in the transaction request tracker also wipes txid requests queued to resolve orphan children. If that parent arrived from a peer that did not announce the orphan child, opportunistic 1P1C relay fails to pair them, the child's announcers are never queried for the parent, and the child remains stuck in the orphanage.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author's functional test demonstration: in p2p_opportunistic_1p1c.py, the new test_parent_from_other_peer times out on master when using a legacy parent (wallet_nonsegwit) waiting for getdata from the child announcer, but passes with this change."
