  "card": "Preserves orphan resolution requests for non-witness transactions during opportunistic 1P1C package relay. For legacy transactions, wtxid equals txid, so calling ForgetTxHash when a parent is rejected as TX_RECONSIDERABLE inadvertently deletes queued txid requests intended to fetch the parent from peers that announced the child. If the low-feerate parent arrived from a peer other than the child's announcer, 1P1C cannot pair them, and the child remains orphaned until re-announced. This change skips ForgetTxHash for non-witness reconsiderable transactions, resolving a test timeout bug and bringing legacy 1P1C handling in line with segwit behavior.",
